A||||6||87GTZ34||Rear brake hose problem||||9||
Z||000000||87GTZ34||09-26-2001||05:34 PM||||This is a pre '88 car.  I started changing all of my brake hoses and of course ran into trouble on the 1st one (right rear).  The frame bracket interlock pattern does not match the replacement hose.  I ordered the hoses from crap-parts.com and got wagner hoses.  I went to a local store and they gave me the same wagner part number but the hose itself was slightly different. O-k-a-y one of them screwed up...  The new hose also has a different interlock pattern that doesn't match my bracket.  What I mean by interlock pattern is that the hose flange has tabs cut into it that are certain sizes and at certain angles.  The bracket has cutouts to accept these tabs.  This system somewhat ensures that no bozo uses the wrong hose on the car and kills themself or someone else.  Anyway, has anyone that has done this recall what tab pattern was cut into the right rear frame bracket?<P>TIA||||reg||9
